---
const faqs = [
  {
    question:
      "Can LKProfessionals host a website developed by another provider?",
    answer:
      "Potentially, yes. We first need to review the application's technology, hosting requirements, dependencies and current configuration.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "What is the difference between web hosting and VPS hosting?",
    answer:
      "Web hosting is generally suited to websites and applications that can operate within a managed hosting environment. VPS hosting provides greater server-level control and is more appropriate where custom software, services or configuration are required.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Who owns the domain if LKP registers it?",
    answer:
      "The business should retain clear ownership of its domain. Registration and administration can be managed by LKP while ownership and account responsibility remain documented.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can you migrate an existing website or email service?",
    answer:
      "Yes, depending on access and the source and destination platforms. Migration work is normally planned to reduce disruption and preserve required data.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Do SSL certificates need renewal?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Certificates have expiry periods. Depending on the environment, renewal can often be automated, but it still needs to be configured and monitored correctly.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Does hosting include backups?",
    answer:
      "Backup requirements depend on the hosting arrangement. We prefer to define backup and recovery expectations explicitly rather than assume that provider-level backups are sufficient for every business system.",
  },
];
---

<section class="cloud-faq">
  <div class="site-container cloud-faq__layout">
    <div>
      <p>Cloud & hosting FAQ</p>

      <h2>
        Questions before placing the system online.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="cloud-faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cloud-faq {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: #ffffff;
  }

  .cloud-faq__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(16rem, 0.68fr)
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 8rem);
  }

  .cloud-faq__layout
    > div:first-child > p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #0b2f8f;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .cloud-faq h2 {
    max-width: 11ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #0d203c;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .cloud-faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid #dce3ec;
  }

  .cloud-faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dce3ec;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .cloud-faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #293b53;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .cloud-faq details p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: #788497;
    font-size: 0.69rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .cloud-faq__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
